ed by IRBP gene sequences</article-title><source>Mol Phylogenet Evol</source><year>2004</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>256</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15019624</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ympev.2003.07.002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>PF</given-names></name><name><surname>McGrath</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruddle</surname><given-names>FH</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruddle</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cloning and expression of murine lymphotoxin cDNA</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><year>1987</year><volume>138</volume><fpage>4496</fpage><lpage>501</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2884262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eck</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ultsch</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rinderknecht</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>de Vos</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sprang</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The structure of human lymphotoxin (tumor necrosis factor-beta) at 1.9-A resolution</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1992</year><volume>267</volume><fpage>2119</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1733919</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Banner</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Arcy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Janes</surname><given-names>W</given-na